G1 Light Sync
=============

Unofficial companion for the Mitsuko Phantom G1. This independent project is
not affiliated with or endorsed by Mitsuko.

Launch “G1 Light Sync” from the applications menu, or run:
  mitsuko-g1

The command-line controller is available as:
  mitsuko-g1ctl info

The package installs the USB udev rule, reloads udev, and adds the sudo
invoking user to plugdev when possible. Reconnect the strip after install.
Log out and back in if group membership was added.

The package includes the Wayland portal helper. Grant monitor access once:
  wayland-screenshot cast enroll --monitor
The desktop portal will show its permission chooser. Music mode only needs
PipeWire playback and does not require screen-capture authorization.

Per-user settings are stored in ~/.config/mitsuko-g1.
